<Page title="How We Verify Updates" description="How ResultDosti collects government job, admit card and result updates from official websites and checks the details before publishing.">
  <h2>1. Official sources only</h2>
  <p>Every update on ResultDosti comes from the official website of the body that published it. We do not copy from other job websites, social media posts or forwarded messages. Each page names its source website and links to it.</p>
  <h2>2. Automatic checks through the day</h2>
  <p>The official notice pages of each body are checked roughly every two hours. When a new notice appears, it is added with the date shown next to it on the official website. If no date is shown there, the page says when ResultDosti found it instead. If a website is down or changes its layout, no new items are added from it until it works again, and the problem is flagged for review.</p>
  <h2>3. Details checked for consistency</h2>
  <p>When a recruitment notification is a readable PDF, dates, fee and age limits are read from it automatically. A value is only shown if it passes basic checks, for example the last date must come after the start date and within a sensible period of the notice date, and fees and ages must be within normal ranges. Values that fail these checks are left out, and the page asks you to read the official notice instead.</p>
  <h2>4. Closing and expiry</h2>
  <p>When the last date of a job could be read, the job is marked closed automatically after that date. Closed jobs stay on their exam page so you can follow the admit card, answer key and result. If the last date could not be read, the page asks you to check it in the official notification.</p>
  <h2>5. Corrections</h2>
  <p>If you find something wrong, write to us from the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with the page link. The official notification is always the final authority.</p>
</Page>
